<StanceStatePage state="ma">
  <p>This webpage houses the responses to 6 questions
    crafted by the Massachusetts Stance on Science team.</p>
    <p>Only official candidates who will appear on ballots were contacted.</p>
    <p>Candidates were contacted in late June 2026 (with a follow-up to those who
    did not initially respond) and given the opportunity to answer all questions. Only the responses of candidates who answered the questions are
    included. None of the candidates' responses were modified in any way before
    being published on this resource page.</p>

    <p><u>For the <strong>2026 Massachusetts elections</strong></u>, only candidates in
    the following elections were contacted<sup>1</sup>:</p>

    <div>
      <details class="stance-race-group">
        <summary>US Senate</summary>
          <ul>
            <li>Democratic and Republican primary candidates</li>
            <li>General election candidates, including independent candidates</li>
          </ul>
      </details>
      <details class="stance-race-group">
        <summary>US House</summary>
          <ul>
            <li>Democratic and Republican primary candidates</li>
            <li>General election candidates, including independent candidates</li>
          </ul>
      </details>
      <details class="stance-race-group">
        <summary>Governor</summary>
          <ul>
            <li>Democratic and Republican primary candidates</li>
            <li>General election candidates, including independent candidates</li>
          </ul>
      </details>
      <details class="stance-race-group">
        <summary>Massachusetts Senate</summary>
          <ul>
            <li>All contested races in the Democratic and Republican primaries</li>
            <li>Independent candidates running in the general election</li>
          </ul>
      </details>
      <details class="stance-race-group">
        <summary>Massachusetts House</summary>
          <ul>
            <li>All contested races in the Democratic and Republican primaries</li>
            <li>Independent candidates running in the general election</li>
          </ul>
      </details>
    </div>
    <p><small><sup>1</sup> These primary elections were prioritized because
    they have more than one official candidate on the ballot.</small></p>

    <p>The contacted candidates include candidates running in the 2026 primary
    and general elections.</p>
</StanceStatePage>
